1
00:00:00,084 --> 00:00:01,501
<i>Previously on</i> Reacher...

2
00:00:01,502 --> 00:00:03,169
Whoever did this weren't amateurs.

3
00:00:03,170 --> 00:00:05,797
ME needs to take a look at the knife
the guy that took a run at me used,

4
00:00:05,798 --> 00:00:07,924
- see if it matches these wounds.
- Okay.

5
00:00:07,925 --> 00:00:09,092
Whatever is on that drive

6
00:00:09,093 --> 00:00:11,344
is the property of the United States Army,

7
00:00:11,345 --> 00:00:14,931
and I just want to see it get returned
to the Pentagon where it belongs.

8
00:00:14,932 --> 00:00:16,891
The jump drive.
Anna had it when she left for Philly.

9
00:00:16,892 --> 00:00:18,476
I think I know where she put it.

10
00:00:18,477 --> 00:00:19,644
She mailed the drive,

11
00:00:19,645 --> 00:00:22,188
and maybe her phone,
before getting on the subway.

12
00:00:22,189 --> 00:00:24,733
A woman kills herself
on the same train as the chief of staff

13
00:00:24,734 --> 00:00:26,526
of a potential presidential candidate.

14
00:00:26,527 --> 00:00:28,611
CIA starts kidnapping people over it.

15
00:00:28,612 --> 00:00:29,738
Let's do it the easy way

16
00:00:29,739 --> 00:00:30,989
- this time, Reacher.
- No.

17
00:00:30,990 --> 00:00:33,117
- [intense music playing]
- [grunting]

18
00:00:36,162 --> 00:00:38,788
It appears Ben's throat was cut
with a curved knife.

19
00:00:38,789 --> 00:00:40,248
<i>Resembles a claw.</i>

20
00:00:40,249 --> 00:00:41,541
It's called a karambit,

21
00:00:41,542 --> 00:00:43,835
<i>used by practitioners
of certain martial arts in Indonesia.</i>

22
00:00:43,836 --> 00:00:45,045
[suspenseful music playing]

23
00:00:50,384 --> 00:00:53,929
Philly PD! Hands up! Hands up!

24
00:00:58,100 --> 00:01:00,102
[sirens wailing in distance]

25
00:01:02,521 --> 00:01:04,355
[officer] Hands behind your head.

26
00:01:04,356 --> 00:01:06,149
- [tense music playing]
- [officer over radio] <i>Alpha Team.</i>

27
00:01:06,150 --> 00:01:07,151
<i>Perimeter secure.</i>

28
00:01:08,152 --> 00:01:09,235
I didn't do this.

29
00:01:09,236 --> 00:01:11,196
Shut the fuck up. On your knees.

30
00:01:11,197 --> 00:01:13,574
<i>Bravo Two, holding position.</i>

31
00:01:15,576 --> 00:01:18,037
[intense music playing]

32
00:01:19,163 --> 00:01:20,163
[gunshot]

33
00:01:20,164 --> 00:01:22,917
- [officer 2] Shots fired.
- [siren wailing]

34
00:01:29,006 --> 00:01:30,883
♪ ♪

35
00:01:46,232 --> 00:01:48,067
[grunting softly]

36
00:01:58,536 --> 00:02:00,538
- [grunting]
- [cloth rips, stops]

37
00:02:04,750 --> 00:02:07,126
[SWAT leader muffled] We need backup
at Liberty Gardens Hotel.

38
00:02:07,127 --> 00:02:09,462
Six bodies, suspect on the run.

39
00:02:09,463 --> 00:02:13,675
Caucasian male, six-four, uh, six-five,
250 pounds,

40
00:02:13,676 --> 00:02:15,427
likely armed.

41
00:02:18,889 --> 00:02:21,308
- [suspenseful music playing]
- [trash chute opens]

42
00:02:25,104 --> 00:02:26,938
[officer over radio] <i>We should move on.</i>

43
00:02:26,939 --> 00:02:28,566
<i>Echo only.</i>

44
00:02:30,109 --> 00:02:31,861
<i>Second floor clear.</i>

45
00:02:39,702 --> 00:02:42,955
[radio transmission echoing]

46
00:02:50,462 --> 00:02:52,464
♪ ♪

47
00:03:03,893 --> 00:03:05,351
[grunts]

48
00:03:05,352 --> 00:03:07,062
[panting]

49
00:03:09,189 --> 00:03:10,357
Oof.

50
00:03:20,743 --> 00:03:22,118
- [phone beeps]
- [horns honking]

51
00:03:22,119 --> 00:03:23,995
[line rings]

52
00:03:23,996 --> 00:03:25,998
[phone ringing]

53
00:03:27,541 --> 00:03:29,584
It's Reacher.

54
00:03:29,585 --> 00:03:31,461
Been trying to call you
for the last 20 minutes.

55
00:03:31,462 --> 00:03:32,629
<i>Thought you might be dead.</i>

56
00:03:32,630 --> 00:03:34,380
Not me, but a lot of other people.

57
00:03:34,381 --> 00:03:37,425
Four Reds and Lila's bodyguards,
all dead in her hotel room.

58
00:03:37,426 --> 00:03:38,676
Cops showed while I was there.

59
00:03:38,677 --> 00:03:40,428
- Shit.
<i>- They think I did it.</i>

60
00:03:40,429 --> 00:03:42,388
Barely got away.

61
00:03:42,389 --> 00:03:44,265
We need to find out
who took Lila and Amisha.

62
00:03:44,266 --> 00:03:47,477
Reacher, I don't think anyone took them.

63
00:03:47,478 --> 00:03:49,812
The bodies you saw,
their throats were slashed?

64
00:03:49,813 --> 00:03:51,981
<i>Thick cuts, like we saw
on the OnlyFans girl?</i>

65
00:03:51,982 --> 00:03:55,610
Yeah. Reds were cut up like that.
How'd you know?

66
00:03:55,611 --> 00:03:58,196
[Tamara] <i>Med examiner said
both Mary Ellen Daniels and Ben</i>

67
00:03:58,197 --> 00:04:01,199
were killed with a curved blade
with a wide tip called a karambit.

68
00:04:01,200 --> 00:04:03,868
<i>A weapon specifically from Indonesia.</i>

69
00:04:03,869 --> 00:04:05,745
Where's your girl from, Reacher?

70
00:04:05,746 --> 00:04:08,206
[intense music playing]

71
00:04:08,207 --> 00:04:10,333
I got it wrong.

72
00:04:10,334 --> 00:04:11,834
[Russell] <i>Lila and Amisha
came back to the room,</i>

73
00:04:11,835 --> 00:04:13,670
<i>found their guards dead
and the Reds waiting for them.</i>

74
00:04:13,671 --> 00:04:16,214
<i>They sliced 'em and ran.
They weren't kidnapped.</i>

75
00:04:16,215 --> 00:04:17,590
[Tamara] <i>They gamed us the whole time.</i>

76
00:04:17,591 --> 00:04:20,385
She and Amisha hired Mary Ellen
to seduce your nephew,

77
00:04:20,386 --> 00:04:22,011
then killed her and abducted Ben.

78
00:04:22,012 --> 00:04:24,222
Anna never would've mailed
that thumb drive to Lila.

79
00:04:24,223 --> 00:04:25,556
She was trying to keep it away from her.

80
00:04:25,557 --> 00:04:27,392
She mailed it to someone else.

81
00:04:27,393 --> 00:04:30,436
Someone who'd do anything to help her,
someone she trusted more than anybody.

82
00:04:30,437 --> 00:04:32,647
<i>Her brother.</i>

83
00:04:32,648 --> 00:04:34,440
That drive could've been sitting

84
00:04:34,441 --> 00:04:36,609
in Jacob's mailbox
since at least this morning.

85
00:04:36,610 --> 00:04:38,528
- You need to go get it. Now.
- [sirens wailing]

86
00:04:38,529 --> 00:04:40,530
- [Tamara] <i>And what are you gonna do?</i>
- Run.

87
00:04:40,531 --> 00:04:42,616
[intense music playing]

88
00:04:43,283 --> 00:04:44,159
Freeze!

89
00:04:48,080 --> 00:04:50,040
- [brakes screech]
- [horn blares]

90
00:04:53,669 --> 00:04:55,044
[grunts]

91
00:04:55,045 --> 00:04:57,006
Don't fucking move!

92
00:05:08,559 --> 00:05:10,561
<i>[thunder rumbling]</i>

93
00:05:21,572 --> 00:05:23,574
[♪ The Plimsouls sing
"Million Miles Away"]

94
00:05:28,829 --> 00:05:31,039
You know, I can drive.

95
00:05:31,040 --> 00:05:32,708
- Maybe you should--
- We're almost there.

96
00:05:34,501 --> 00:05:36,377
<i>♪ Friday night, I'd just got back...</i>

97
00:05:36,378 --> 00:05:38,629
Gives me something to focus on.

98
00:05:38,630 --> 00:05:40,674
<i>♪ was dreaming about the past...</i>

99
00:05:41,675 --> 00:05:42,759
But thanks for offering.

100
00:05:42,760 --> 00:05:44,343
[Russell] Oh, man.

101
00:05:44,344 --> 00:05:46,554
- What?
- Well, I asked some trusted sources

102
00:05:46,555 --> 00:05:49,307
from the dark web if they could dig up
anything on Amisha and Lila.

103
00:05:49,308 --> 00:05:53,895
Amisha's a ghost, but a financial hacker
I know just found something on Lila.

104
00:05:53,896 --> 00:05:55,313
Scrooge McFuck?

105
00:05:55,314 --> 00:05:58,274
That's just his handle. All right?
He's totally trustworthy,

106
00:05:58,275 --> 00:06:01,360
and he discovered that,
up until a few weeks ago,

107
00:06:01,361 --> 00:06:04,113
Lila Hoth had zero economic fingerprint.

108
00:06:04,114 --> 00:06:06,574
She had no mortgages, bank accounts,
student loans, not even a credit score.

109
00:06:06,575 --> 00:06:11,245
That's because the names Lila Hoth
and Amisha Hoth are bullshit.

110
00:06:11,246 --> 00:06:13,706
Exactly. But then, out of nowhere,

111
00:06:13,707 --> 00:06:15,708
a Platinum Amex card under Lila's name

112
00:06:15,709 --> 00:06:17,668
with a six-figure limit
shows up in the system.

113
00:06:17,669 --> 00:06:20,213
A few weeks ago, she uses it
to buy first-class plane tickets

114
00:06:20,214 --> 00:06:23,966
from Indonesia to the U.S. for Lila Hoth,
Amisha Hoth, and their two bodyguards.

115
00:06:23,967 --> 00:06:26,010
Then, more recently, she bought

116
00:06:26,011 --> 00:06:29,055
a fifth ticket for a flight from Djibouti
that landed here this morning.

117
00:06:29,056 --> 00:06:30,932
- Who's from Djibouti?
- [Russell] I don't know.

118
00:06:30,933 --> 00:06:32,475
McFuck's running a trace
on that ticket now,

119
00:06:32,476 --> 00:06:35,269
but whatever name he comes up with,
it's gonna be a fake, bogus passport,

120
00:06:35,270 --> 00:06:37,230
but... [scoffs]

121
00:06:37,231 --> 00:06:40,191
...the Hoths obviously brought this guy
into the U.S. to do something.

122
00:06:40,192 --> 00:06:43,569
Well, whatever it is, it's not good.

123
00:06:43,570 --> 00:06:46,572
<i>♪ There was no one around,
to the place that ♪</i>

124
00:06:46,573 --> 00:06:48,575
[birds singing]

125
00:06:53,163 --> 00:06:55,748
We'll be right back.
Keep doing your thing.

126
00:06:55,749 --> 00:06:57,876
Roger that.

127
00:07:08,679 --> 00:07:10,556
[tense, suspenseful music playing]

128
00:07:11,515 --> 00:07:12,724
This is Anna's handwriting.

129
00:07:20,274 --> 00:07:21,941
There you are, you little fucker.

130
00:07:21,942 --> 00:07:23,485
[soft chuckle]

131
00:07:36,665 --> 00:07:38,416
Her phone.

132
00:07:38,417 --> 00:07:40,377
011806.

133
00:07:41,378 --> 00:07:44,089
- Ben's birthday.
- She gave you her password.

134
00:07:45,966 --> 00:07:47,134
What's this?

135
00:07:48,302 --> 00:07:50,803
Tomas Waberi.

136
00:07:50,804 --> 00:07:52,431
What are you up to?

137
00:07:53,223 --> 00:07:54,141
[Jacob] It's dead.

138
00:07:55,434 --> 00:07:58,020
[sighs] And my charger isn't compatible.

139
00:07:59,021 --> 00:08:01,480
We'll buy you a new one,
but for right now,

140
00:08:01,481 --> 00:08:03,984
let's get that drive into Plum's laptop.

141
00:08:05,235 --> 00:08:07,111
[engine revs]

142
00:08:07,112 --> 00:08:08,446
Tamara.

143
00:08:08,447 --> 00:08:10,031
That car.

144
00:08:10,032 --> 00:08:12,116
[intense music playing]

145
00:08:12,117 --> 00:08:13,660
[Tamara] Go!

146
00:08:15,787 --> 00:08:17,915
Go. Go. Go, go, go, go!

147
00:08:26,298 --> 00:08:27,966
[line ringing]

148
00:08:30,552 --> 00:08:31,928
[dispatch over phone] <i>911.
What's your emergency?</i>

149
00:08:31,929 --> 00:08:34,513
This is Detective Tamara Green
with the Philadelphia PD.

150
00:08:34,514 --> 00:08:37,016
I'm with a Mayfield police officer
and a civilian

151
00:08:37,017 --> 00:08:39,727
in an unmarked blue Ford Taurus
headed north on...

152
00:08:39,728 --> 00:08:41,979
- Where the fuck are we?
- Parsons Avenue.

153
00:08:41,980 --> 00:08:43,397
Parsons Ave. Black SUV

154
00:08:43,398 --> 00:08:45,149
<i>with two armed adult females</i>

155
00:08:45,150 --> 00:08:47,194
<i>in active pursuit of our vehicle.</i>

156
00:08:48,028 --> 00:08:49,446
We need backup now!

157
00:08:50,030 --> 00:08:51,113
Help!

158
00:08:51,114 --> 00:08:53,032
[dispatch] <i>Copy, Detective.
We're sending units your way.</i>

159
00:08:53,033 --> 00:08:54,451
<i>Please stay on the line.</i>

160
00:09:08,340 --> 00:09:09,341
[grunts]

161
00:09:21,395 --> 00:09:22,312
[speaking Indonesian]
Don't let them get away.

162
00:09:22,437 --> 00:09:23,062
Won't happen.

163
00:09:23,063 --> 00:09:23,772
Go faster!

164
00:09:28,026 --> 00:09:29,820
Hold on. I'm gonna try something.

165
00:09:34,992 --> 00:09:36,994
[engine revving]

166
00:09:38,578 --> 00:09:40,538
Whoa, whoa, you're going too fast.
We're gonna wind up in the river.

167
00:09:40,539 --> 00:09:43,082
Rite of passage in high school
to make this turn at full speed.

168
00:09:43,083 --> 00:09:45,335
We all did it. Lila didn't.

169
00:09:55,429 --> 00:09:56,929
Holy shit.

170
00:09:56,930 --> 00:09:58,764
I thought you made this turn
in high school?

171
00:09:58,765 --> 00:10:00,851
I did, and I slammed my dad's Maxima
right into the bridge.

172
00:10:07,733 --> 00:10:10,109
[dramatic music playing]

173
00:10:10,110 --> 00:10:11,278
They crashed.

174
00:10:11,945 --> 00:10:13,739
[brakes screeching]

175
00:10:29,796 --> 00:10:31,589
We still got trouble.

176
00:10:31,590 --> 00:10:34,300
[Lila screams, pants]

177
00:10:34,301 --> 00:10:36,136
[suspenseful music playing]

178
00:10:43,727 --> 00:10:45,812
We've got the flash drive,
and their ride is shot.

179
00:10:46,688 --> 00:10:49,440
Drive away before we all end up dead.

180
00:10:49,441 --> 00:10:52,443
If we run, they'll run, too.

181
00:10:52,444 --> 00:10:54,862
I'm keeping them on the bridge
until backup gets here.

182
00:10:54,863 --> 00:10:56,364
They got automatic weapons.

183
00:10:56,365 --> 00:10:58,532
If you don't like
what I'm about to do...

184
00:10:58,533 --> 00:10:59,659
get out.

185
00:11:08,710 --> 00:11:09,794
Be smart.

186
00:11:09,795 --> 00:11:12,881
You haven't lost what I've lost.

187
00:11:28,980 --> 00:11:30,774
I only got seven rounds left.

188
00:11:34,694 --> 00:11:36,112
So let's make 'em count.

189
00:11:36,113 --> 00:11:38,907
[intense music playing]

190
00:11:40,450 --> 00:11:42,452
[gunfire]

191
00:11:50,001 --> 00:11:51,002
Ah!

192
00:11:55,298 --> 00:11:56,758
[both grunt]

193
00:12:11,398 --> 00:12:12,816
I'm sorry.

194
00:12:15,402 --> 00:12:17,904
[siren wailing in distance]

195
00:12:29,166 --> 00:12:30,584
We have to go!

196
00:12:30,834 --> 00:12:33,003
No, they have the drive!

197
00:12:33,170 --> 00:12:35,297
We can't sell anything if we're dead!

198
00:12:39,593 --> 00:12:40,510
Lila!

199
00:12:40,802 --> 00:12:41,470
Now!

200
00:12:41,761 --> 00:12:43,305
Fuck! [screams]

201
00:12:44,681 --> 00:12:47,558
[officer] Get off the railing
and onto the ground.

202
00:12:47,559 --> 00:12:51,271
- No. No! No!
- What?

203
00:13:02,449 --> 00:13:03,532
No!

204
00:13:03,533 --> 00:13:06,410
- [officer] Show me your hands!
- Philly PD!

205
00:13:06,411 --> 00:13:09,122
- Philly PD!
- They got away!

206
00:13:10,749 --> 00:13:12,917
From this height,
there's a good chance they're dead.

207
00:13:12,918 --> 00:13:14,210
[officer] Hands!

208
00:13:14,211 --> 00:13:15,920
[gun cocks]

209
00:13:15,921 --> 00:13:17,172
Toss the badge.

210
00:13:21,384 --> 00:13:23,386
[low, dramatic music playing]

211
00:13:44,199 --> 00:13:46,201
[door closes in distance]

212
00:13:55,877 --> 00:13:57,295
[door opens]

213
00:14:00,006 --> 00:14:01,508
[door closes]

214
00:14:03,885 --> 00:14:06,429
[footsteps approaching]

215
00:14:13,562 --> 00:14:16,272
You know, this isn't the first time
Green's been caught up in trouble.

216
00:14:16,273 --> 00:14:18,148
And the first time
wasn't her fault, either.

217
00:14:18,149 --> 00:14:20,651
Screwed by some political burn job.

218
00:14:20,652 --> 00:14:23,904
Now, the kid's getting the high hard one
again, thanks to you.

219
00:14:23,905 --> 00:14:25,573
Oh, it's my fault?

220
00:14:25,574 --> 00:14:30,327
She's good police. I always figured,
soon enough, she'd find her old gear

221
00:14:30,328 --> 00:14:33,539
and climb out of the hole she got kicked
into, but then, you come along,

222
00:14:33,540 --> 00:14:35,374
drag her into this bullshit.

223
00:14:35,375 --> 00:14:38,168
And now, you're worried she'll be working
with some washed-up,

224
00:14:38,169 --> 00:14:40,297
bullshit, half-in-the-bag cop forever.

225
00:14:43,091 --> 00:14:44,634
That I am.

226
00:14:45,510 --> 00:14:48,679
Speaking of bullshit, want to explain why

227
00:14:48,680 --> 00:14:54,310
Giant Boxcar Willie's got the personal
cell number of a presidential candidate?

228
00:14:54,311 --> 00:14:57,521
And don't tell me it's fake.
I called and hung up,

229
00:14:57,522 --> 00:15:00,649
guy who answered sounded
just like the one I've seen on TV.

230
00:15:00,650 --> 00:15:03,945
What the hell
do you have Tamara tied up in?

231
00:15:05,405 --> 00:15:07,114
If I tell you, will you help me?

232
00:15:07,115 --> 00:15:08,699
Fuck no.

233
00:15:08,700 --> 00:15:11,244
Then shove that card up your ass.

234
00:15:21,838 --> 00:15:23,213
[door opens]

235
00:15:23,214 --> 00:15:24,715
[sighs]

236
00:15:24,716 --> 00:15:25,674
[door closes]

237
00:15:25,675 --> 00:15:26,842
[entry bell jingles]

238
00:15:26,843 --> 00:15:29,345
Yeah, got the biggest one they had.

239
00:15:29,346 --> 00:15:31,221
I'll pick up ice cream on the way home.

240
00:15:31,222 --> 00:15:35,142
I know, but no tonsils
equals a lot of spoiling.

241
00:15:35,143 --> 00:15:37,269
[chuckles] Okay.

242
00:15:37,270 --> 00:15:39,063
See you soon.

243
00:15:39,064 --> 00:15:41,232
- Love you, too.
- [woman] Excuse me, sir?

244
00:15:42,817 --> 00:15:44,610
[choking]

245
00:15:44,611 --> 00:15:46,196
[tense music playing]

246
00:16:04,464 --> 00:16:06,465
- All right. That should do it.
- [clears throat]

247
00:16:06,466 --> 00:16:10,344
Just treat it with antibiotic ointment
twice a day for three days,

248
00:16:10,345 --> 00:16:11,970
- should be good.
- All right.

249
00:16:11,971 --> 00:16:13,348
Thanks, Terry.

250
00:16:20,730 --> 00:16:24,024
[Russell] Look, the screen is busted.
There's no way we're gonna be able to read

251
00:16:24,025 --> 00:16:25,150
the drive on this thing.

252
00:16:25,151 --> 00:16:26,694
District hardware's a no-go.

253
00:16:26,695 --> 00:16:30,781
The less they o-or anyone else knows
about this drive, the better.

254
00:16:30,782 --> 00:16:33,784
- So, this stays between us and Reacher.
- Okay.

255
00:16:33,785 --> 00:16:35,495
I should check in with him.

256
00:16:36,705 --> 00:16:38,164
[knock on door]

257
00:16:39,791 --> 00:16:41,251
- Yeah?
- [door opens]

258
00:16:43,420 --> 00:16:44,796
Jakey?

259
00:16:48,717 --> 00:16:50,301
We're ok, Unc.

260
00:16:51,678 --> 00:16:54,430
I was in Hackensack when I got the call
about the bridge.

261
00:16:54,431 --> 00:16:56,516
First Anna, now this?

262
00:16:58,226 --> 00:17:02,062
Guys, this is, uh,
Lieutenant Monty DeRosa.

263
00:17:02,063 --> 00:17:03,480
He keeps the Mayfield station running.

264
00:17:03,481 --> 00:17:06,650
Uncle Monty, this is Detective
Tamara Green and Russell Plum.

265
00:17:06,651 --> 00:17:08,902
- They're friends of mine.
- [Russell] So...

266
00:17:08,903 --> 00:17:11,280
policing, what, it's a family business?

267
00:17:11,281 --> 00:17:12,698
[chuckles]

268
00:17:12,699 --> 00:17:14,533
I was his dad's partner for years.

269
00:17:14,534 --> 00:17:17,537
He's been calling me uncle
since he was a kid. [chuckles]

270
00:17:18,705 --> 00:17:22,082
With everything that's happening, I don't
see how you're even still standing.

271
00:17:22,083 --> 00:17:24,002
I mean, I can barely function.

272
00:17:26,045 --> 00:17:28,173
How-How's Ben holding up?

273
00:17:29,257 --> 00:17:31,341
[somber music playing]

274
00:17:31,342 --> 00:17:32,843
Ben... [exhales]

275
00:17:32,844 --> 00:17:35,263
Ben was murdered, Unc.

276
00:17:36,473 --> 00:17:37,474
Oh, God.

277
00:17:40,852 --> 00:17:43,103
What the hell's going on here, son?

278
00:17:43,104 --> 00:17:45,397
We don't know yet,

279
00:17:45,398 --> 00:17:47,232
but the two women
who jumped off the bridge,

280
00:17:47,233 --> 00:17:48,651
they're behind all of it.

281
00:17:54,783 --> 00:17:56,074
Yeah, I know it's a lot.

282
00:17:56,075 --> 00:17:58,119
Yeah, it-it's more than you realize.

283
00:17:59,871 --> 00:18:02,539
Those women are not done killing.

284
00:18:02,540 --> 00:18:05,167
[suspenseful music playing]

285
00:18:05,168 --> 00:18:06,211
Meaning?

286
00:18:07,462 --> 00:18:08,671
Merle Harkavey.

287
00:18:09,798 --> 00:18:14,092
He was found dead.
Jugular slashed over on Pleasant Avenue,

288
00:18:14,093 --> 00:18:17,262
and a witness said they saw
two soaking wet women

289
00:18:17,263 --> 00:18:19,557
jump in his car and drive off.

290
00:18:23,436 --> 00:18:24,729
They're alive.

291
00:18:25,730 --> 00:18:27,732
[siren wailing in distance]

292
00:18:53,800 --> 00:18:55,384
You fish your gun out?

293
00:18:55,385 --> 00:18:56,594
Nah.

294
00:19:00,265 --> 00:19:03,393
Got an oldie but a goodie right here.

295
00:19:06,062 --> 00:19:08,647
You know, you should've
gone with me in Baltimore.

296
00:19:08,648 --> 00:19:11,191
- Now, the rules have changed.
- Let me guess.

297
00:19:11,192 --> 00:19:13,652
Real cops are gonna
find me hanging dead in here

298
00:19:13,653 --> 00:19:16,947
'cause I couldn't take the guilt
from all those things I didn't do.

299
00:19:16,948 --> 00:19:18,240
That's about right.

300
00:19:18,241 --> 00:19:20,242
So, cry to your God.

301
00:19:20,243 --> 00:19:22,160
Scream for help.

302
00:19:22,161 --> 00:19:24,746
Nobody's gonna hear you
through the cinderblock.

303
00:19:24,747 --> 00:19:26,373
Oh.

304
00:19:26,374 --> 00:19:29,376
There was something else

305
00:19:29,377 --> 00:19:32,046
that I was supposed to tell you.

306
00:19:36,718 --> 00:19:38,510
You lose, Reacher.

307
00:19:38,511 --> 00:19:39,845
[gun cocks]

308
00:19:39,846 --> 00:19:42,473
[intense music playing]

309
00:19:43,016 --> 00:19:44,809
[grunts, shouts]

310
00:19:48,771 --> 00:19:50,773
[screaming]

311
00:19:59,741 --> 00:20:03,244
[whimpering]

312
00:20:04,037 --> 00:20:06,455
- You son of a bitch.
- You'll be fine.

313
00:20:06,456 --> 00:20:08,166
I knew a kid in Maine who was missing one.

314
00:20:09,167 --> 00:20:11,168
He turned out okay.

315
00:20:11,169 --> 00:20:12,294
No.

316
00:20:12,295 --> 00:20:14,504
No, no, no, no, no. [grunts]

317
00:20:14,505 --> 00:20:16,507
[dramatic music playing]

318
00:20:31,064 --> 00:20:32,482
[Reacher exhales]

319
00:20:39,656 --> 00:20:42,074
We can't bring the Feds in.

320
00:20:42,075 --> 00:20:44,618
- Just trust me on this, please.
- [Monty] This is not about trust.

321
00:20:44,619 --> 00:20:45,827
This is about reality.

322
00:20:45,828 --> 00:20:48,830
This case is too goddamn big
for the Mayfield police department.

323
00:20:48,831 --> 00:20:51,375
The Feds will take over.
They will box me out.

324
00:20:51,376 --> 00:20:53,877
They have the resources to deal
with this kind of thing.

325
00:20:53,878 --> 00:20:55,295
It is my family that they murdered!

326
00:20:55,296 --> 00:20:58,590
I'm taking these animals in,
not the fucking Feds.

327
00:20:58,591 --> 00:21:01,218
[Monty] These are stone-cold killers.

328
00:21:01,219 --> 00:21:03,136
Have you seen what they've been doing?

329
00:21:03,137 --> 00:21:06,723
They're dropping bodies right and left.
They're shooting at police officers.

330
00:21:06,724 --> 00:21:09,810
This is out of our league.
This is a federal matter.

331
00:21:09,811 --> 00:21:12,771
You call the FBI,
you tell 'em what you know,

332
00:21:12,772 --> 00:21:14,482
and you let them do their job.

333
00:21:15,650 --> 00:21:17,276
Okay, Unc.

334
00:21:18,653 --> 00:21:22,656
We have reason to believe the Feds
might be trying to cover this up, okay?

335
00:21:22,657 --> 00:21:25,575
CIA is part of it, too. I...

336
00:21:25,576 --> 00:21:27,536
I didn't want to tell you.

337
00:21:27,537 --> 00:21:28,830
I don't want you involved.

338
00:21:29,914 --> 00:21:31,498
Why would the government do that?

339
00:21:31,499 --> 00:21:32,916
We're not sure.

340
00:21:32,917 --> 00:21:34,584
Which branch of the Feds is it?

341
00:21:34,585 --> 00:21:36,378
- We have no idea.
- [Monty] You don't know.

342
00:21:36,379 --> 00:21:39,297
[sighs] Jake.

343
00:21:39,298 --> 00:21:43,176
You are too smart to hang your hat
on a bunch of question marks.

344
00:21:43,177 --> 00:21:45,762
You don't know who. You don't know why.

345
00:21:45,763 --> 00:21:49,434
You just think that
the Feds might be involved?

346
00:21:50,518 --> 00:21:52,185
That's all you got?

347
00:21:52,186 --> 00:21:53,771
[distant chatter]

348
00:21:58,943 --> 00:21:59,944
Okay.

349
00:22:01,279 --> 00:22:03,113
All right. I'll call them. I'll...

350
00:22:03,114 --> 00:22:04,448
- Good boy.
- I'll fill 'em in on everything.

351
00:22:04,449 --> 00:22:06,700
- [Monty] Good.
- Come on, man. You--

352
00:22:06,701 --> 00:22:08,535
No, no, no, no, no.
We are a demoted detective,

353
00:22:08,536 --> 00:22:10,788
a small-town cop, and a goddamn blogger.

354
00:22:18,087 --> 00:22:20,213
- We're in over our heads.
- [Monty] That's right.

355
00:22:20,214 --> 00:22:22,216
That's a good boy. You call 'em.

356
00:22:23,342 --> 00:22:25,635
[sighs] Now, I'm hungry.

357
00:22:25,636 --> 00:22:27,929
I'm gonna order some food.
You guys look like you could use it.

358
00:22:27,930 --> 00:22:29,474
[door opens]

359
00:22:38,900 --> 00:22:41,152
I'm not calling the fucking FBI.

360
00:22:43,196 --> 00:22:44,863
[Monty] All right, once more for safety.

361
00:22:44,864 --> 00:22:49,951
Fifteen cheese, 15 no onions,
three bags of fries, six-pack of Cokes.

362
00:22:49,952 --> 00:22:51,995
- Charge it to the PD account.
- [cashier] <i>Copy that.</i>

363
00:22:51,996 --> 00:22:53,830
Okay, thanks.

364
00:22:53,831 --> 00:22:54,915
- [cashier] <i>Sure thing.</i>
- [call ends]

365
00:22:54,916 --> 00:22:56,208
Hey, the FBI will be here in an hour,

366
00:22:56,209 --> 00:22:58,002
and we're just gonna step outside
for some air.

367
00:22:59,128 --> 00:23:01,421
- Hell of a day.
- [Monty] Well, take your time.

368
00:23:01,422 --> 00:23:04,008
Just ordered White Manna.
Should be here in a bit.

369
00:23:05,635 --> 00:23:07,385
Thanks.

370
00:23:07,386 --> 00:23:08,596
I appreciate it.

371
00:23:17,939 --> 00:23:19,565
<i>[line ringing]</i>

372
00:23:25,321 --> 00:23:26,780
Still no answer.

373
00:23:26,781 --> 00:23:28,116
Think someone maybe got him?

374
00:23:29,742 --> 00:23:31,119
I don't know.

375
00:23:34,247 --> 00:23:36,206
[phone rings]

376
00:23:36,207 --> 00:23:37,667
[phone beeps]

377
00:23:38,376 --> 00:23:39,835
- Hello?
- [Reacher over phone] <i>It's me.</i>

378
00:23:39,836 --> 00:23:42,504
[Tamara] <i>What the hell happened to you?</i>

379
00:23:42,505 --> 00:23:45,006
Cops arrested me, but I got out.

380
00:23:45,007 --> 00:23:46,383
[Tamara] <i>What do you mean "got out"?</i>

381
00:23:46,384 --> 00:23:48,802
Means I'm stacking up charges.
You get the drive?

382
00:23:48,803 --> 00:23:51,680
And Anna's phone, but it's dead,
and my laptop was shot.

383
00:23:51,681 --> 00:23:53,890
- Shot?
- [Tamara] <i>Lila and Amisha wound up</i>

384
00:23:53,891 --> 00:23:55,934
at Jacob's. We got away,
but they know we have the drive.

385
00:23:55,935 --> 00:23:57,018
Where are you now?

386
00:23:57,019 --> 00:23:58,436
Heading to Philly in Jacob's cruiser.

387
00:23:58,437 --> 00:24:00,105
Stolen cruiser.

388
00:24:00,106 --> 00:24:01,606
[Reacher] Lila and Amisha?

389
00:24:01,607 --> 00:24:03,650
[Russell] <i>Looking for us.
They're looking for the drive.</i>

390
00:24:03,651 --> 00:24:06,737
[Tamara] <i>In a car they jacked in Mayfield.
Sliced a man's throat to get it.</i>

391
00:24:08,281 --> 00:24:10,824
- Is he alive?
- [Jacob] <i>Merle bled out on the street.</i>

392
00:24:10,825 --> 00:24:12,033
<i>He was a good man.</i>

393
00:24:12,034 --> 00:24:14,244
Had three daughters.

394
00:24:14,245 --> 00:24:16,955
There's a BOLO, but Lila'll swap out
cars if she hasn't already.

395
00:24:16,956 --> 00:24:19,040
I'm sorry, but where are we going?

396
00:24:19,041 --> 00:24:21,793
If Lila and Amisha are after us,
and the Philly cops are after Reacher...

397
00:24:21,794 --> 00:24:23,378
And the CIA.

398
00:24:23,379 --> 00:24:25,380
They're gonna be pissed
after what I just did.

399
00:24:25,381 --> 00:24:26,715
[Tamara] <i>Stay in the city and lie low.</i>

400
00:24:26,716 --> 00:24:30,093
We'll meet at the corner of G Street
and East Allegheny,

401
00:24:30,094 --> 00:24:31,928
one block east of K and A.

402
00:24:31,929 --> 00:24:35,182
No police stations in the area, and
there's an electronics store on the corner

403
00:24:35,183 --> 00:24:37,309
so we can grab a charger
and a new laptop.

404
00:24:37,310 --> 00:24:39,561
- How far out are you?
- [Tamara] <i>We'll be there in</i>

405
00:24:39,562 --> 00:24:40,854
70 minutes.

406
00:24:40,855 --> 00:24:42,939
Make it 90.

407
00:24:42,940 --> 00:24:45,275
The sliders should be getting
to the station soon.

408
00:24:45,276 --> 00:24:48,279
Monty'll come looking for us,
see that we took off and put out an alert.

409
00:24:49,363 --> 00:24:51,073
We gotta ditch this cruiser.

410
00:24:52,825 --> 00:24:54,159
- [♪ Mykal sings "No Reason"]
- <i>♪ having a reason ♪</i>

411
00:24:54,160 --> 00:24:55,994
<i>♪ She say that she love me,
but only want money ♪</i>

412
00:24:55,995 --> 00:24:57,996
<i>♪ I switch out my bread like the season ♪</i>

413
00:24:57,997 --> 00:25:00,081
<i>♪ I always stunt on the 'gram,
I just buy what I want ♪</i>

414
00:25:00,082 --> 00:25:02,042
<i>♪ You gonna know when you see me,
I always...</i>

415
00:25:02,043 --> 00:25:03,835
You got to be shittin' me.

416
00:25:03,836 --> 00:25:05,921
<i>♪ I live like a boss, and I mean it,
back on my bully...</i>

417
00:25:05,922 --> 00:25:08,798
Stay by the car. What up, Cyrus?

418
00:25:08,799 --> 00:25:10,050
How's the cat?

419
00:25:10,051 --> 00:25:12,844
The cat? Tore up my sister's BarcaLounger.

420
00:25:12,845 --> 00:25:14,554
Now she says I got to get her a new one.

421
00:25:14,555 --> 00:25:17,098
So, if y'all came to give me a puppy,
get gone.

422
00:25:17,099 --> 00:25:19,184
No pets this time. Need a ride.

423
00:25:19,185 --> 00:25:21,144
- You got a ride.
- That's staying here.

424
00:25:21,145 --> 00:25:22,812
You ain't leaving no fucking
cop car at my spot.

425
00:25:22,813 --> 00:25:25,023
Park it out back and throw a tarp over it.

426
00:25:25,024 --> 00:25:27,692
<i>♪ at you, at you,
Skittles got me feeling sick...</i>

427
00:25:27,693 --> 00:25:29,110
Or I could just seize everything in here

428
00:25:29,111 --> 00:25:31,112
that doesn't have a bill of sale,
down to the last hubcap.

429
00:25:31,113 --> 00:25:35,158
<i>♪ As long as the 80 is loaded and my
fingers rolling, then we gonna be rich ♪</i>

430
00:25:35,159 --> 00:25:36,785
<i>♪ My life is different...</i>

431
00:25:36,786 --> 00:25:37,994
[sighs]

432
00:25:37,995 --> 00:25:40,038
Shit, man. Why you always trying
to fuck with my pocket?

433
00:25:40,039 --> 00:25:43,000
<i>♪ but only want money,
I switch out my bread like the season ♪</i>

434
00:25:55,888 --> 00:25:58,307
[vehicle approaching]

435
00:26:07,024 --> 00:26:08,358
Nice ride.

436
00:26:08,359 --> 00:26:11,027
Got it from an old friend.

437
00:26:11,028 --> 00:26:14,948
So, you want to tell us how you got out
of Philly PD custody?

438
00:26:14,949 --> 00:26:16,951
[Muzak playing]

439
00:26:24,542 --> 00:26:27,128
- The entire ear?
- [elevator bell dings]

440
00:26:35,011 --> 00:26:36,762
Not this one.

441
00:26:37,888 --> 00:26:39,348
[elevator bell dings]

442
00:26:45,229 --> 00:26:46,731
Not this one, either.

443
00:26:47,606 --> 00:26:49,775
[elevator doors slide closed]

444
00:26:50,901 --> 00:26:52,069
[elevator bell dings]

445
00:26:55,948 --> 00:26:57,241
This'll work.

446
00:27:02,621 --> 00:27:04,999
[speaking Spanish]
How'd you like to make some extra cash?

447
00:27:06,876 --> 00:27:07,877
Do you speak English?

448
00:27:08,085 --> 00:27:09,587
A little...

449
00:27:09,795 --> 00:27:11,838
You're cleaning this room
hours after final checkout,

450
00:27:11,839 --> 00:27:13,798
so you're not rushing to get it ready
for the next occupant.

451
00:27:13,799 --> 00:27:17,345
No harm in letting us use it
for a few hours.

452
00:27:19,347 --> 00:27:20,598
Everybody wins.

453
00:27:28,272 --> 00:27:30,191
You're braver than I am.

454
00:27:35,071 --> 00:27:36,113
[computer beeps]

455
00:27:36,781 --> 00:27:38,616
All right, let's take a look.

456
00:27:47,500 --> 00:27:49,542
Sampson, Cahill.

457
00:27:49,543 --> 00:27:51,711
That must be General Putra.

458
00:27:51,712 --> 00:27:53,756
- What the fuck is this?
- [phone chimes]

459
00:27:56,008 --> 00:27:56,926
It's charged.

460
00:27:58,219 --> 00:28:01,471
[Reacher] I said I'd know what to do with
the drive once I saw what was on it, but

461
00:28:01,472 --> 00:28:02,764
I don't even know what I'm looking at.

462
00:28:02,765 --> 00:28:06,351
We have mercenaries, Feds, the CIA, and
Indonesian killers all after this thing,

463
00:28:06,352 --> 00:28:08,770
and we still don't know why.
There are no other files on here.

464
00:28:08,771 --> 00:28:11,356
- None of this makes any sense.
- Why would anyone kill over this?

465
00:28:11,357 --> 00:28:14,609
I found Anna's last text chain.
It was with a blocked number.

466
00:28:14,610 --> 00:28:16,236
That's got to be Lila.

467
00:28:16,237 --> 00:28:19,198
She sent Anna an address in Philly
the night she died.

468
00:28:20,157 --> 00:28:21,533
Where they were supposed to meet.

469
00:28:21,534 --> 00:28:23,118
That's where we're headed to next.

470
00:28:23,119 --> 00:28:26,330
190 East... 190 East...

471
00:28:30,292 --> 00:28:32,669
First floor is an abandoned restaurant.

472
00:28:32,670 --> 00:28:35,547
Looks like it's under
some kind of renovation.

473
00:28:35,548 --> 00:28:38,133
Lila sent a video...

474
00:28:38,134 --> 00:28:39,635
right before the address.

475
00:28:43,305 --> 00:28:45,307
- No.
- Jacob...

476
00:28:47,184 --> 00:28:49,602
- [Ben over video] <i>Stop.</i>
- [Mary screaming over video]

477
00:28:49,603 --> 00:28:53,357
- [Ben] <i>Please stop!</i>
- [Lila] <i>Tell your mother.</i>

478
00:28:55,109 --> 00:28:57,486
<i>Mom, they're cutting her up.</i>

479
00:28:58,487 --> 00:29:00,322
<i>They say I'm next
if you don't do what they say.</i>

480
00:29:02,283 --> 00:29:04,702
<i>Stop. Please.</i>

481
00:29:09,415 --> 00:29:10,416
There's another one.

482
00:29:14,128 --> 00:29:16,629
Don't see what you can't unsee.

483
00:29:16,630 --> 00:29:18,591
[tense music playing]

484
00:29:24,597 --> 00:29:27,223
Hey. He shouldn't be out there alone.

485
00:29:27,224 --> 00:29:28,600
He's not gonna jump.

486
00:29:28,601 --> 00:29:30,311
I just think someone should be with him.

487
00:29:35,065 --> 00:29:37,484
Keep checking the phone,
see if you can find anything useful.

488
00:29:37,485 --> 00:29:39,569
[bird singing]

489
00:29:39,570 --> 00:29:41,572
[traffic passing below]

490
00:29:50,456 --> 00:29:52,124
I'm gonna hurt them...

491
00:29:53,709 --> 00:29:55,752
...like they hurt my family.

492
00:29:55,753 --> 00:29:59,255
I will take their knives

493
00:29:59,256 --> 00:30:04,093
and dig them deep into their guts.

494
00:30:04,094 --> 00:30:06,888
Slaughter them

495
00:30:06,889 --> 00:30:08,933
like the animals they are.

496
00:30:12,686 --> 00:30:14,395
I don't know you very well,

497
00:30:14,396 --> 00:30:17,023
but I know that's not who you are.

498
00:30:17,024 --> 00:30:19,401
That's not the person
Anna and Ben loved.

499
00:30:22,404 --> 00:30:24,949
That person's as dead as they are.

500
00:30:42,508 --> 00:30:44,510
I won't let you spin out.

501
00:30:46,428 --> 00:30:48,638
[news anchor over TV] <i>A breaking story
now. Police are urging</i>

502
00:30:48,639 --> 00:30:51,724
<i>citizens of Philadelphia
and the Delaware Valley area</i>

503
00:30:51,725 --> 00:30:53,977
<i>to be on the lookout for this man,
who assaulted</i>

504
00:30:53,978 --> 00:30:57,814
<i>a police officer and escaped custody
just hours ago.</i>

505
00:30:57,815 --> 00:31:01,651
{\an8}<i>The fugitive, Jack Reacher,
was apprehended earlier today</i>

506
00:31:01,652 --> 00:31:03,653
{\an8}<i>in relation to multiple homicides.</i>

507
00:31:03,654 --> 00:31:09,033
<i>He's described as a white male,
six-foot-five, and 250 pounds.</i>

508
00:31:09,034 --> 00:31:11,995
<i>At over six-foot-three inches
and 250 pounds...</i>

509
00:31:11,996 --> 00:31:14,205
- [phone chiming and buzzing]
<i>- ...Jack Reacher is considered to be</i>

510
00:31:14,206 --> 00:31:16,374
<i>extremely dangerous.</i>

511
00:31:16,375 --> 00:31:19,627
- [TV turns off]
- [phone continues chiming and buzzing]

512
00:31:19,628 --> 00:31:21,255
- Here we go.
- [phone beeps]

513
00:31:22,256 --> 00:31:25,049
You are all over the fucking news,
so this better be good.

514
00:31:25,050 --> 00:31:28,970
Why are people dying over a photo of you,
Cahill, and Putra from over 25 years ago?

515
00:31:28,971 --> 00:31:31,055
So, you found the drive.

516
00:31:31,056 --> 00:31:32,473
Is that what was on it?

517
00:31:32,474 --> 00:31:33,891
A photo?

518
00:31:33,892 --> 00:31:35,018
[Reacher] <i>And nothing else.</i>

519
00:31:35,019 --> 00:31:37,395
<i>As far as I can tell,
it's nothing worth killing over.</i>

520
00:31:37,396 --> 00:31:39,230
Well, it's got to be blackmail, then.

521
00:31:39,231 --> 00:31:42,942
Evidence of collaboration with Putra
would be a blow to my campaign.

522
00:31:42,943 --> 00:31:47,280
Bullshit. I already told you, bin Laden
and Hussein were our allies once.

523
00:31:47,281 --> 00:31:51,075
Plenty of politicians cozied up to them
without losing their careers over it.

524
00:31:51,076 --> 00:31:53,036
And no offense,
that's a hell of a lot of carnage

525
00:31:53,037 --> 00:31:54,662
just to derail a congressman
from North Carolina.

526
00:31:54,663 --> 00:31:57,541
Then I don't know what's special
about that photograph.

527
00:32:00,711 --> 00:32:02,629
Maybe the other guy in the photo does.

528
00:32:02,630 --> 00:32:04,298
- Show him.
- Yeah, sure.

529
00:32:08,385 --> 00:32:09,552
[laptop whooshes]

530
00:32:09,553 --> 00:32:10,888
[phone chimes]

531
